        "workup_and_crystallization": "Cool to room temperature; collect orange crystals, wash twice with 5 mL CH3CN, dry under vacuum.",
        "yield": "ca. 19% (based on Sm(NO3)3·9H2O)"
      },
      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "First reported Sm(III) SMM: frequency-dependent out-of-phase ac signal centered near 1.5 K; Arrhenius barrier Ueff = 16 K and τ0 = 2e-8 s. Magnetization hysteresis at 0.5 K with a zero-field step attributed to QTM. χMT(300 K) = 21.3 cm3 K mol-1, slightly below the Fe12 plus four isolated Sm(III) expectation, indicating Sm–Sm and possibly Sm–Fe coupling. M vs H at 2 K overlaps the Fe12La4 analogue, consistent with antiferromagnetic Sm coupling to an S = 8 Fe12 ground state.",
        "measurements": [
