        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Diamagnetic La(III) analogue used as a Fe12-core reference. Dominant antiferromagnetic Fe–Fe coupling: χMT(300 K) = 22.5 vs 52.5 cm3 K mol-1 expected for 12 uncoupled Fe(III). χMT stays near 21.3 at 150 K, rises to 36.3 at 15 K, then drops, indicating mixed ferro/antiferromagnetic interactions and a nonzero ground state. Magnetization at 2 K tends to 16.4 Nβ at 50 kOe, modeled by a Brillouin curve for S = 8, g = 2.0. No out-of-phase ac signal.",
